# Expo apps: Universal + responsive layout (hard)

Applies to **`xituan_app_merchant`** and **`xituan_app_customer`** only.

## Chosen delivery model

**One App per product** (iOS + iPadOS + Android), **responsive layout** via breakpoints / column count / optional content max-width.

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| Single Expo project per app; Universal iPhone+iPad | Separate phone vs tablet App Store binaries |
| Shared screens + `ResponsiveCardGrid` / width-driven columns | Hardcode `width: '48%'` / single-column image grids on phone |
| `useWindowDimensions` / `onLayout` for available width | Assume phone-only (~390pt) when building lists/cards |
| Prefer readable density (min card ~168, max ~4 cols) | Pack as many columns as possible on iPad landscape |

Defer a full “tablet shell” (persistent sidebar + split panes) until product asks for it — still **one App**, not a second target.

## Do not copy phone-only references as the wide-layout source of truth

When the work **involves layout** (lists, grids, forms, sheets, split panes, max content width), **do not** treat existing implementations as sufficient for iPad / large Android just because they “match reference”:

| Reference | Typical width assumption |
|-----------|--------------------------|
| WeChat mini-program | Phone only |
| CMS / Site **mobile** mode | Phone only — not tablet / wide breakpoints |

**Required:** before implementing or porting layout from those sources, **ask the developer** whether this screen needs **explicit tablet / wide consideration** (columns, content max-width, denser chrome, etc.), instead of silently cloning phone layout.

- Business / interaction parity with WeChat or CMS is still fine to follow.
- **Visual grid / width / chrome density on large screens** is a separate decision — confirm when unsure.

## Image / activity / product card grids

Reuse each app’s `ResponsiveCardGrid` + `RESPONSIVE_CARD_GRID` (keep merchant ↔ customer constants aligned):

- `MIN_COLUMNS = 2` (phone)
- `MIN_CARD_WIDTH ≈ 168`, `GAP = 10`, `MAX_COLUMNS = 4`
- Card root width `100%` **inside** grid cells (do not nest another `%` column)

```tsx
// BAD — phone-only 2-up, ignores iPad
<View style={{ flexDirection: 'row', flexWrap: 'wrap', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
  <Card style={{ width: '48%' }} />
</View>

// GOOD
<ResponsiveCardGrid
  items={rows.map((row) => ({
    key: row.id,
    node: <Card {...row} /> // card width: '100%'
  }))}
/>
```

## Checklist before shipping UI

- [ ] If layout was ported from WeChat / CMS / Site mobile: asked whether tablet / wide needs separate treatment
- [ ] Phone portrait: ≥2 columns for image-card grids
- [ ] Tablet / wide: more columns without tiny unreadable tiles
- [ ] Forms / detail: readable line length (consider max content width / padding), not stretched edge-to-edge on iPad
- [ ] No new “iPad-only app” or duplicate layout tree unless explicitly requested
